{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record shows both endpoints were amended after booking: the pickup was moved from Blk 118 Rivervale Dr, Sengkang to Punggol MRT PHV Pickup Bay at 07:12:30 (pickup_amended_at), and the dropoff was changed from Changi T1 Departure Door 3 to Changi T3 Departure Door 7 at 07:41:52 (dropoff_amended_at). Under POL-RD-05 the POL-RD-01 threshold test must therefore be re-applied against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints - trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km of 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min of 31.0, both stored fields and both non-null - and not against the 21.0 km booked T1 route that the rider's receipt quotes. The rider's 'usually 21 km' figure is the superseded pre-amendment baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured against the amended baseline the excess is 26.17 km of governing trace distance (gps_trace.trace_distance_km) less the 24.60 km amended optimal, i.e. about 1.57 km, which is roughly 6.4% of the amended optimal route. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds 20% of optimal_distance_km AND exceeds 0.8 km absolute, and both tests must pass. The percentage gate fails decisively on the amended figure, so no deviation is established on this trip and the outcome is NO_ACTION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both amendments were the rider's own doing and sit verbatim in the chat log: at 07:11:58 she wrote 'im at punggol mrt phv pickup bay instead, moved the pin', which the driver acknowledged at 07:12:15, and at 07:41:40 she wrote 'sorry ah can change to T3? my friend flight is T3 not T1', which the driver acknowledged at 07:42:05. The additional distance and the terminal change the rider now complains of are rider-caused, which is precisely the situation POL-RD-05 addresses - a rider moving the pin and a rider giving a different destination in the chat_log.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own complaint that the driver 'drove around the airport for another five minutes' is the circling at the amended T3 dropoff - a point she had only just moved to, at which the driver reports she was not at the kerb. POL-RD-05 excludes exactly this distance: where the rider was not at the amended point and the gps_trace shows the vehicle circling within 400 m of it for more than 4 minutes, that circling distance is also excluded from excess. The admissibility note on EV-GPS-00108 records two loops of the T3 departure kerb well inside 380 m of the amended pin, and the rider's own account of about five minutes of circling corroborates the duration. I note that derived.arrival is unavailable on this bundle because trip_record.pickup_zone_class is null, so this point rests on the trace summary and the rider's own admission rather than on a computed dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold. On the amended route the excess is 1.57 km and 6.4%, which does not meet that threshold, so the burden never shifts to the driver and no exculpatory clause needs to be reached. The rider's assertion that the trip 'is usually about 21 km' measures against the superseded booked route rather than the amended endpoints actually driven, which is a wrong-field comparison and fails on that ground alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 206 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps list and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. None of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs (a) to (c) is met, so no independent corroboration requirement attaches and the trace's own distance figure governs the POL-RD-01 test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "coverage_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern is established against this driver. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 402, a ratio of 0.00, far below the 0.05 limb of POL-RD-06, and the 3-or-more limb is not met either. POL-RD-06 therefore supplies no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral on this record. I flag for the Judge that driver_profile.prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is NOT the trailing-90-day field POL-RD-06 names, so it cannot be substituted for it under POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity defect that could add to the rider's side. The fare breakdown carries no airport surcharge, which is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, and the ERP totals are zero with no gantry lines charged. POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom line and no wrongly applied surcharge to bite on, and the fare lines reconcile to the cent against a charged_total of SGD 33.77.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic advisory artifact is absent from the pool and carries weight 0.0, so the POL-RD-03 closure exoneration is not available to the driver on this record. That absence is immaterial here: no road closure is put in issue by either party, the driver does not rely on POL-RD-03, and the case is decided on the amended endpoints under POL-RD-05. The missing artifact cuts neither way.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00108-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

