    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you — here is what the record shows and why no money moves.\n\nThe receipt is for the trip as originally booked: Blk 118 Rivervale Dr to Changi Terminal 1, an optimal 21.0 km. But the trip was not driven that way, because the rider changed it. At 07:11:58 she messaged that she had moved the pickup pin to Punggol MRT PHV Pickup Bay (driver acknowledged 07:12:15), and at 07:41:40 she asked to change the destination from Terminal 1 to Terminal 3 (acknowledged 07:42:05). The trip record carries both amendments — pickup_amended_at 07:12:30 and dropoff_amended_at 07:41:52 — and the platform's re-quote for the amended endpoints, amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0.\n\nPOL-RD-05 therefore applies: where the trip record shows the pickup or dropoff was amended after booking, the deviation test is re-run against the optimal route between the amended endpoints. POL-RD-01 itself defines optimal distance as the booked figure 'or the adjusted optimal produced by ... POL-RD-05 ... where one of those clauses applies', so this is a measurement rule that follows from the record rather than a defence the driver must separately plead; the driver's case also cites EV-TRIP-00108 and EV-CHAT-00108 for POL-RD-05.\n\nRunning the test on the amended route: the governing GPS trace is 26.17 km (EV-GPS-00108 — 206 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, empty gaps list, so it is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 and its figure governs over the rounded 26.2 km receipt line, which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test). The excess over the amended optimal is 26.17 - 24.60 = 1.57 km, which is 6.4% of 24.60 km. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be both more than 20% of the optimal and more than 0.8 km; the 0.8 km limb passes but the 20% limb fails, so no deviation is established and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION. The rider's 'usually about 21 km' compares against the superseded pre-amendment route and is not the right baseline. Her account of the driver 'driving around the airport' does not help her either: she was not at the amended T3 pin, and POL-RD-05 excludes circling within 400 m of the amended point for more than 4 minutes, which on this record only reduces the excess further.\n\nOn the remaining points: the rider is right that POL-RD-04 is unavailable — waypoint_hint is null on all four messages, so its corroboration test cannot be run — but the driver does not rely on POL-RD-04 and the outcome does not turn on it. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 402), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. The fare breakdown reconciles to the cent: no airport surcharge (correct — this trip ends at Changi, it does not originate there) and no ERP gantry lines, so no billing-integrity correction arises under POL-RD-09(4). The driver billed 26.2 km against a 26.17 km trace, so there is no unbilled distance and no driver compensation under POL-RD-04. The traffic-advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is missing (weight 0.0), but no closure is in issue and POL-RD-03 plays no part.\n\nThe charge of SGD 33.77 stands. fare_breakdown.payment_status remains CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd remains SGD 0.00."
  },
