    "explanation": "Both of you: the ride was booked from Blk 118 Rivervale Drive to Changi Terminal 1 on a 21.0 km optimal route, but the trip as actually requested was different, and the record shows who changed it. Before the vehicle set off, the rider moved the pickup pin to Punggol MRT (pickup_amended_at 07:12:30; chat 07:11:58 'im at punggol mrt phv pickup bay instead, moved the pin', acknowledged by the driver at 07:12:15). On the way in she changed the destination to Terminal 3 (dropoff_amended_at 07:41:52; chat 07:41:40 'sorry ah can change to T3? my friend flight is T3 not T1', acknowledged at 07:42:05). The platform re-quoted the route between those amended endpoints, and that re-quote is a stored field on the trip record: amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0 (EV-TRIP-00108).\n\nPOL-RD-05 requires the deviation test to be re-run against the amended 24.60 km baseline. The governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km 26.17 km (EV-GPS-00108), not the rounded 26.2 km receipt line, which POL-RD-01 says may not be cited for the test. The excess is therefore 26.17 - 24.60 = 1.57 km, which is 6.4% of 24.60 km. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds BOTH 20% of the optimal route and 0.8 km absolute. The 6.4% percentage gate fails, so no deviation is established and no refund is due. The rider's 'usually 21 km' baseline is the superseded pre-amendment route; measuring against it yields 5.17 km / 24.6% (EV-GPS-00108), but that comparison is the wrong one once the rider's own requested changes are on the record.\n\nThe rider argues that POL-RD-05 is an exculpatory clause the driver never invoked, so the trace deviation should stand. I do not accept that. The amendments are not the driver's assertion: they are recorded by the platform on the trip record (both amendment timestamps, both pre-amendment endpoints, and the re-quote) and are confirmed by the rider's own chat messages. POL-RD-01 itself directs the baseline to be the adjusted optimal produced by POL-RD-05 where that clause applies, and POL-RD-05 applies on the face of the record. The rider's separate point that POL-RD-04 is unavailable because waypoint_hint is null is correct but immaterial: this case does not turn on POL-RD-04.\n\nThe rider's complaint about roughly five minutes of circling near Terminal 3 does not change the outcome. POL-RD-05 excludes, from excess, circling within 400 m of the amended dropoff; here the excess is already below the POL-RD-01 threshold before any such exclusion, so nothing turns on it. (I note derived.arrival is unavailable on this bundle because trip_record.pickup_zone_class is null, so no computed dwell exists; none is needed.)\n\nNo billing-integrity correction arises under POL-RD-09(4). The fare lines reconcile to the cent against charged_total SGD 33.77 (EV-FARE-00108); ERP and tolls are 0.00 with no gantry lines charged; and no airport surcharge is applied, which is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there. No POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over 402 completed trips in 90 days), so no conduct referral fires, and no POL-GEN-03 referral is produced by any clause.\n\nResult: the charge stands as billed. NO_ACTION leaves fare_breakdown.payment_status and refund_issued_sgd as they are; no amount is refunded to the rider and no compensation is due to the driver. Confidence rests on the trip record, GPS trace and chat log, each at weight_multiplier 1.0. Two claims resting on the missing traffic-advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00108-01 were discarded at the mechanical check for not disclosing its zero weight; no closure is in issue, so they do not affect this outcome."
