    "explanation": "To both parties — this dispute is decided under POL-RD-05 (pickup or dropoff point relocation), and the outcome is NO_ACTION: the charge stands.\n\nThe trip you were charged for was not the trip as first booked. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00108) shows the pickup was amended from Blk 118 Rivervale Dr, Sengkang to Punggol MRT PHV Pickup Bay at 07:12:30, and the dropoff was amended from Changi T1 Departure Door 3 to Changi T3 Departure Door 7 at 07:41:52. Both amendments were the rider's own doing and sit verbatim in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00108): 'im at punggol mrt phv pickup bay instead, moved the pin' at 07:11:58 and 'sorry ah can change to T3? my friend flight is T3 not T1' at 07:41:40, each acknowledged by the driver. Under POL-RD-05 the POL-RD-01 threshold test must be re-run against the platform's optimal route between the amended endpoints, stored on the record as amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km (duration 31.0 min, amended_optimal_duration_min). The 21.0 km booked route the receipt quotes is the superseded pre-amendment baseline.\n\nMeasured against 24.60 km, the governing trace distance (EV-GPS-00108, gps_trace.trace_distance_km 26.17 km) gives an excess of 1.57 km, i.e. about 6.4% of the amended optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds 20% of the optimal distance AND exceeds 0.8 km absolute — both tests must pass. The percentage gate is not met, so no deviation survives the recomputation and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION. The roughly five minutes spent circling the T3 kerb is separately excluded under POL-RD-05's circling provision; I note that the computed arrival/dwell fact is unavailable because trip_record.pickup_zone_class is null, so that exclusion rests on the trace summary and the rider's own account rather than a computed dwell.\n\nThe rider's claims are answered. The claim that the derived geometry records the deviation as ESTABLISHED (5.17 km / 24.62%) is rejected: that derivation was run against the booked 21.0 km optimal, which POL-RD-05 supersedes; the derived status is not a substitute for applying the clause. The point that gps_trace.trace_distance_km 26.17 km governs over the rounded receipt line of 26.2 km is accepted, but it changes nothing. The claim that the rider's initial burden is discharged is accepted, but the corrected optimal figure means the threshold excess is not there once the baseline is fixed. The claim that POL-RD-05 'is invoked nowhere' by the driver is rejected: the driver's brief invokes POL-RD-05 and names the artifacts (EV-TRIP-00108, EV-GPS-00108, EV-CHAT-00108) and the clause, which is what POL-RD-08 asks of it; and in any event POL-RD-05 operates on the amendment timestamps the record itself carries. The rider's acceptance that the amended-baseline excess is 1.57 km / 6.4% and below threshold is correct and is the basis of this ruling. The rider-profile point (deviation_claims_60d of 1, so no extra corroboration under POL-RD-08) is accepted and does not affect the result. POL-RD-04's rider-requested-detour limb does not help the driver, because waypoint_hint is null on every message, but nothing turns on it here.\n\nOn the money: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00108) is a metered fare with charged_total SGD 33.77, no airport surcharge (correct — the trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there) and zero ERP, so POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom line or wrongly applied surcharge to bite on and no billing-integrity referral arises. No repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 402 completed trips in 90 days, so POL-RD-06 gives neither a FULL_REFUND uplift nor a conduct referral; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the field POL-RD-06 names and was not used. No driver compensation arises under POL-RD-04 — the fare breakdown billed 26.2 km against a trace of 26.17 km, so there is no unbilled shortfall. The GPS trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (206 fixes, 10 s interval, 100% coverage, empty gaps), so no corroboration requirement attached and no escalation is engaged under POL-RD-10. Charged total SGD 33.77; amount refunded SGD 0.00; driver compensation SGD 0.00.",
